Subject: fuji_reset_ptp: free the previous priv struct instead of leaking it

The condition was inverted (`if (r->priv == NULL) free(r->priv)`), so a
reset leaked the old struct PtpUserPriv. Harmless for the first reset (priv
is NULL after ptp_init) but every later reset leaked.

--- a/libfuji/fuji.c
+++ b/libfuji/fuji.c
@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@
 
 int fuji_reset_ptp(struct PtpRuntime *r) {
 	ptp_reset(r);
-	if (r->priv == NULL) free(r->priv);
+	if (r->priv != NULL) free(r->priv);
 	r->priv = calloc(1, sizeof(struct PtpUserPriv));
 	r->connection_type = PTP_IP_USB;
 	r->response_wait_default = 3; // Fuji cams are slow!
